EA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA MASAHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, HAJIME</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, MASAHITO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO HAJIME</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA MASAHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, HAJIME</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, MASAHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of converting at least one aromatic compound selected among (a) an aromatic compound having three or more substituents, (b) an aromatic compound having two substituents at least one of which is a halogen or has two or more carbon atoms, and (c) a substituted naphthalene or anthracene derivative, characterized by contacting the aromatic compound with a catalyst comprising a zeolite characterized in that (1) the main channels thereof have a minimum inlet diameter larger than 0.65 nm or a maximum inlet diameter larger than 0.70 nm and (2) the main channels each does not intersect a void larger than a ten-membered oxygen ring. By the method, an aromatic compound having a relatively large molecular size can be efficiently converted.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de transformer au moins un composé aromatique. Ce composé est sélectionné parmi (a) un composé aromatique comportant trois ou plusieurs substituants, (b) un composé aromatique comportant deux substituants dont au moins un est un halogène, et qui comporte deux oulusieurs atomes de carbone et (c) un dérivé de naphthalène ou d'anthracène. Ce procédé se caractérise en ce qu'il consiste à placer le composé aromatique en contact avec un catalyseur comprenant unzéolite dont (1) les principaux canaux présentent un diamètre minimal d'entrée de 0,65 nm ou un diamètre maximal d'entrée de 0,70 nm, et (2) les principaux canaux ne recoupent pas un vide plus large qu'une chaîne d'oxygène à 10 éléments. Ce procédé permet de conférer une grande taille moléculaire à un composé aromatique qui peut ensuite être aisément transformé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>